---
// Two-panel diagram for emergent fact discovery.
// Panel 1 — the bridge: facts about different subjects in two similarity
//   clusters that name the same motif, with no similarity edge between them
//   (review's far lane); the keystone E the model may propose sits beneath.
//   A shared domain or entity does not qualify a bridge (knomit #125); it only
//   breaks ties in the rank order.
// Panel 2 — the two directions: near motif lane → consequence, far motif lane
//   (high effort only) → keystone. Both are served by knomit_review.
// Built in the RequestFlow.astro vocabulary: inline SVG over theme vars,
// surface-1 fills, colour-coded hairlines, mono labels.
//   clusters/known = --k-ref (blue) · the bridge signal = --k-brand (green)
//   the discovered keystone/hypothesis = --k-temporal (amber)
interface Props {
  compact?: boolean;
}
const { compact = false } = Astro.props;
---

<figure class="bd">
  <svg
    class="bd__svg"
    viewBox="0 0 720 300"
    fill="none"
    xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
    role="img"
    aria-label="Two similarity clusters of facts, each connected within itself, are linked only by a single shared motif: fact A in one cluster and fact B in the other name the same mechanism, though no similarity edge joins them. That is the bridge. Beneath it sits an unstated keystone E, a premise both facts would rest on, which the model may propose as a hypothesis."
  >
    <defs>
      <marker id="bd-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8.5" refY="5" markerWidth="6.5" markerHeight="6.5" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="var(--k-brand, #77cc99)" />
      </marker>
      <filter id="bd-glow" x="-40%" y="-40%" width="180%" height="180%">
        <feGaussianBlur stdDeviation="4" result="b" />
        <feMerge><feMergeNode in="b" /><feMergeNode in="SourceGraphic" /></feMerge>
      </filter>
    </defs>

    <!-- cluster regions (x/width mirror the panel-2 tile columns below) -->
    <rect class="bd__region" x="24" y="40" width="244" height="94" rx="12" />
    <rect class="bd__region" x="452" y="40" width="244" height="94" rx="12" />
    <text aria-hidden="true" class="bd__region-label" x="146" y="32" text-anchor="middle">similarity cluster A</text>
    <text aria-hidden="true" class="bd__region-label" x="574" y="32" text-anchor="middle">similarity cluster B</text>

    <!-- intra-cluster edges (what similarity sees) -->
    <g class="bd__intra">
      <line x1="74" y1="72" x2="120" y2="62" />
      <line x1="120" y1="62" x2="104" y2="112" />
      <line x1="74" y1="72" x2="104" y2="112" />
      <line x1="120" y1="62" x2="236" y2="86" />
      <line x1="646" y1="72" x2="600" y2="62" />
      <line x1="600" y1="62" x2="616" y2="112" />
      <line x1="646" y1="72" x2="616" y2="112" />
      <line x1="600" y1="62" x2="484" y2="86" />
    </g>

    <!-- the bridge (a motif shared across clusters) -->
    <line class="bd__bridge" x1="236" y1="86" x2="484" y2="86" marker-start="url(#bd-arrow)" marker-end="url(#bd-arrow)" />
    <text aria-hidden="true" class="bd__bridge-label" x="360" y="76" text-anchor="middle">shared motif</text>
    <text aria-hidden="true" class="bd__bridge-sub" x="360" y="106" text-anchor="middle">motif · different clusters</text>

    <!-- cluster A dots -->
    <circle class="bd__dot" cx="74" cy="72" r="6" />
    <circle class="bd__dot" cx="120" cy="62" r="6" />
    <circle class="bd__dot" cx="104" cy="112" r="6" />
    <circle class="bd__dot bd__dot--face" cx="236" cy="86" r="8" />
    <text aria-hidden="true" class="bd__dot-label" x="236" y="122" text-anchor="middle">fact A</text>

    <!-- cluster B dots -->
    <circle class="bd__dot" cx="646" cy="72" r="6" />
    <circle class="bd__dot" cx="600" cy="62" r="6" />
    <circle class="bd__dot" cx="616" cy="112" r="6" />
    <circle class="bd__dot bd__dot--face" cx="484" cy="86" r="8" />
    <text aria-hidden="true" class="bd__dot-label" x="484" y="122" text-anchor="middle">fact B</text>

    <!-- implication lines to the keystone (start below the fact labels) -->
    <g class="bd__imply">
      <path d="M236 134 C252 192 322 224 360 244" />
      <path d="M484 134 C468 192 398 224 360 244" />
    </g>

    <!-- keystone E -->
    <rect class="bd__keystone" x="276" y="244" width="168" height="44" rx="10" filter="url(#bd-glow)" />
    <text aria-hidden="true" class="bd__keystone-title" x="360" y="263" text-anchor="middle">E — keystone</text>
    <text aria-hidden="true" class="bd__keystone-sub" x="360" y="278" text-anchor="middle">unstated · origin: discovered</text>
  </svg>

  <figcaption class="bd__cap">
    Similarity joins each fact to its neighbours, and nothing joins fact A to
    fact B. They are about different subjects, but both name the same
    <strong>motif</strong>: the same mechanism or failure shape. That shared motif
    is the <strong>bridge</strong>. The <strong>keystone</strong> is a premise the
    bridged facts would all rest on, which nobody wrote down because it
    underwrites things that look unrelated.
  </figcaption>

  {!compact && (
    <div class="bd__panel2">
      <div class="bd__dir">
        <span class="bd__dir-tag k-mono bd__dir-tag--fwd">forward · knomit_review, near lane</span>
        <span class="bd__dir-flow k-mono">&#123;A, B, C&#125; &rarr; E</span>
        <span class="bd__dir-note">a <strong>consequence</strong> that follows from the bridged facts but none states alone &rarr; new <code>synthesis</code></span>
      </div>
      <div class="bd__dir">
        <span class="bd__dir-tag k-mono bd__dir-tag--bwd">backward · knomit_review at high, far lane</span>
        <span class="bd__dir-flow k-mono">E &rarr; &#123;A, B, C&#125;</span>
        <span class="bd__dir-note">an unstated <strong>premise</strong> that, if false, breaks them &rarr; new <code>hypothesis</code>, kept only if it reaches enough live dependents</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  )}
</figure>

<style>
  .bd {
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    background: var(--k-surface-1, #1a1a1a);
    border: 1px solid var(--k-hairline-soft, #262626);
    border-radius: var(--k-radius, 12px);
    padding: 1.25rem 1.25rem 1rem;
  }
  .bd__svg { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; overflow: visible; }

  .bd__region {
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--k-ref, #88aaff) 5%, transparent);
    stroke: var(--k-hairline, #333);
    stroke-width: 1.25;
    stroke-dasharray: 4 4;
  }
  .bd__region-label,
  .bd__dot-label {
    font-family: var(--k-font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: 8.5px;
    fill: var(--k-text-muted, #666);
  }
  .bd__intra line { stroke: var(--k-ref, #88aaff); stroke-width: 1; opacity: 0.4; }
  .bd__dot { fill: var(--k-surface-1, #1a1a1a); stroke: var(--k-ref, #88aaff); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .bd__dot--face { stroke-width: 2; }

  .bd__bridge { stroke: var(--k-brand, #77cc99); stroke-width: 2; }
  .bd__bridge-label {
    font-family: var(--k-font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: 10px; font-weight: 600; fill: var(--k-brand, #77cc99);
  }
  .bd__bridge-sub {
    font-family: var(--k-font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: 7.5px; fill: var(--k-text-muted, #666);
  }

  .bd__imply path { stroke: var(--k-temporal, #e5a23c); stroke-width: 1.25; stroke-dasharray: 3 3; opacity: 0.7; }
  .bd__keystone { fill: var(--k-surface-1, #1a1a1a); stroke: var(--k-temporal, #e5a23c); stroke-width: 2; }
  .bd__keystone-title {
    font-family: var(--k-font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; fill: var(--k-temporal, #e5a23c);
  }
  .bd__keystone-sub {
    font-family: var(--k-font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: 7.5px; fill: var(--k-text-muted, #666);
  }

  .bd__cap {
    margin-top: 0.9rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem; line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--k-text-muted, #666); text-align: center;
  }
  .bd__cap strong { color: var(--k-text-2, #aaa); }

  .bd__panel2 {
    display: flex;
    align-items: stretch;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin-top: 1.1rem;
    padding-top: 1.1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--k-hairline-soft, #262626);
  }
  .bd__dir {
    flex: 1 1 0;
    min-width: 0;
    margin: 0; /* override Starlight prose sibling margins (* + *) on docs pages */
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem;
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--k-hairline, #333);
    border-radius: var(--k-radius, 12px);
    background: var(--k-bg, #111);
  }
  .bd__dir-tag { font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .bd__dir-tag--fwd { color: var(--k-brand, #77cc99); }
  .bd__dir-tag--bwd { color: var(--k-temporal, #e5a23c); }
  .bd__dir-flow { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--k-text, #eee); }
  .bd__dir-note { font-size: 0.78rem; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--k-text-muted, #666); }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .bd { padding: 1rem 0.6rem 0.75rem; }
    .bd__panel2 { flex-direction: column; }
    .bd__cap { font-size: 0.74rem; }
  }
</style>
